# LAB10d: a live run on e1m2, the player's own eye. `camera player`, the game's own
# physics, bob and gun sway, `cmd +forward` from file second 0.85 and one `look` line per
# 60 fps frame (a hand's yaw in minimum-jerk strokes), never a path. From the east room
# the player runs west up the steps into the square hall, turns 90 degrees left into the
# rose-window hall (shot 0.8 to 1.2), steps east past the grunt who patrols it, with a
# glance at him (he walks on and does not fire: `notarget`, the film's default), and runs
# on toward the arch under the window, at 320 units a second through the whole shot. Full
# slop, the status bar scaled and overlaid, the gun, crosshair 1, Brightness 0.7. 2.9 s
# with a second of handle each end. The marks m0 to m3 (far points, for measuring the eye)
# and g (the grunt) are never drawn.
#
# Under V3-41, "It's fast, and it feels fast. Mouse-look, W A S D, a gamepad, a phone:
# even a zoomer can play it.", on "It's fast, and it feels fast."

map e1m2

duration 4.9
fps 60
size 1920x1080

preset slop
hud on
gun on
crosshair 1
cvar gamma 0.7

player 1540,680,340,180
camera player

look 0,180
cmd +forward at 0.85
cmd -forward at 4.6
cmd +moveleft at 2.45
cmd -moveleft at 2.8
cmd +moveright at 3.15
cmd -moveright at 3.4
look 0,180.061 at 1.8167
look 0,180.458 at 1.8333
